# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canon EDSDK  --  NON-NEGOTIABLE
#
# Canon licenses EDSDK per developer and forbids redistribution. Headers,
# binaries and the reference manual must never enter this repository or its
# history. Keep your copy outside the repo, or in ./edsdk_sdk/ which is ignored.
#
# The binary patterns below are deliberately broad. Forcing an explicit
# allow-list later is far cheaper than letting a Canon binary slip in once.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Whole-directory rules first: an unpacked SDK archive contains readme text,
# release notes and Canon's sample projects, none of which match a binary or
# header pattern. Ignoring the unpack root is what actually keeps them out.
# The bare-directory rules are ANCHORED with a leading slash, and must stay
# that way. Unanchored, `EDSDK/` matches at any depth -- and because git on
# Windows compares ignore rules case-insensitively, it silently swallowed our
# own source package `src/cefs/edsdk/`, native layer and all. A negation cannot
# rescue it either: git does not descend into an excluded directory. Anchoring
# still protects an SDK unpacked at the repository root, which is the case
# these rules exist for.
edsdk_sdk/
EDSDK_v*/
EDSDK_*_Windows/
EDSDK_*_Mac*/
/EDSDK/
/EDSDK_64/
/Dll/
/Header/
/Library/
*.dll
*.dylib
*.so
*.so.*
*.framework/
*.lib
*.exp
EDSDK*.h
EdsStrings*
*EDSDK*Reference*
*EDSDK*API*
*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets & local config  --  NON-NEGOTIABLE
# config.yaml holds the path to your EDSDK copy. Never commit it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
config.yaml
*.local.*
.env
.env.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# User captures / scans  --  NON-NEGOTIABLE
# Your negatives are yours. They do not belong in a public repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
captures/
scans/
rolls/
*.CR2
*.CR3
*.cr2
*.cr3
# HEIF: what an EOS R7 writes when image quality is set to HEIF rather than
# RAW or JPEG. Easy to miss, and just as much a personal scan as a .CR3.
*.HIF
*.hif
*.HEIF
*.heif
*.HEIC
*.heic
*.tif
*.tiff
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.dng
*.png
# Allow-list for project assets we *do* want tracked.
!docs/**/*.png
!docs/**/*.jpg
!tests/fixtures/**/*.png
!src/cefs/app/static/**/*.png
!src/cefs/app/static/**/*.svg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spike output  --  v0.0 measurements are notes, not artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
spike_output/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
ROADMAP.md
CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md